---
import Base       from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import Nav        from "../../components/Nav.astro";
import PageHero   from "../../components/PageHero.astro";
import ValueStrip from "../../components/ValueStrip.astro";
import Footer     from "../../components/Footer.astro";

const title = "ZeroTier Alternative for Branch Networks: MeshWG vs ZeroTier";
const description = "Compare ZeroTier's Layer 2 network virtualization with MeshWG's Layer 3 router-based WireGuard deployments. Explore pricing, architecture, and router compatibility.";
const canonical = "https://meshwg.com/alternatives/zerotier/";
const publishedTime = "2026-09-16T00:00:00Z";
const modifiedTime  = "2026-09-16T00:00:00Z";

const faqs = [
  {
    q: "What is the architectural difference between MeshWG and ZeroTier?",
    a: "ZeroTier is a Layer 2 network virtualization platform that emulates an Ethernet switch. MeshWG uses WireGuard, which is a Layer 3 IP routing protocol."
  },
  {
    q: "Does MeshWG support broadcast and multicast traffic like ZeroTier?",
    a: "No. Because ZeroTier emulates Layer 2, it supports broadcast and multicast traffic for legacy protocols (like mDNS or BACnet). WireGuard operates at Layer 3, meaning it routes IP packets and does not natively pass broadcast traffic, making it suited for modern IP workloads."
  },
  {
    q: "How does pricing compare between ZeroTier and MeshWG?",
    a: "ZeroTier's Essential plan starts at $18/month (including 10 devices) and charges $2.00 per month for each additional device. MeshWG charges a flat rate per machine/router, regardless of the number of users connecting through it."
  }
];

const faqSchema = { 
  "@context": "https://schema.org", 
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": faqs.map((f) => ({ 
    "@type": "Question", 
    "name": f.q, 
    "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": f.a } 
  })) 
};

const breadcrumbSchema = { 
  "@context": "https://schema.org", 
  "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
  "itemListElement": [
    { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://meshwg.com/" },
    { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Alternatives", "item": "https://meshwg.com/alternatives/" },
    { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3, "name": "ZeroTier", "item": canonical }
  ] 
};
---

<Base title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical}
      ogType="website" publishedTime={publishedTime} modifiedTime={modifiedTime}>
  <Nav />
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="/ alternatives · zerotier"
    title="ZeroTier Alternative for Branch Networks"
    lede="ZeroTier provides Layer 2 network virtualization, while MeshWG uses Layer 3 WireGuard routing. Understand the architectural, pricing, and hardware compatibility differences."
  />
  <ValueStrip />

  <section class="guide">
    <div class="wrap">
      <aside class="toc">
        <div class="toc-h">In this guide</div>
        <ol>
          <li><a href="#layer2-vs-layer3">Layer 2 vs Layer 3</a></li>
          <li><a href="#performance">Performance & Architecture</a></li>
          <li><a href="#router-support">Router Compatibility</a></li>
          <li><a href="#financials">Pricing Models</a></li>
          <li><a href="#faq">FAQ</a></li>
        </ol>
      </aside>

      <article>
        <h2 id="layer2-vs-layer3">Layer 2 vs Layer 3</h2>
        <p>The most fundamental difference between ZeroTier and MeshWG (which uses WireGuard) is the networking layer they operate on.</p>
        <p><strong>ZeroTier is a Layer 2 network virtualization platform</strong> that emulates an Ethernet switch. Because it emulates Layer 2, it supports broadcast and multicast traffic natively. This is necessary if you rely on legacy protocols, mDNS, BACnet, or specific industrial protocols that require a shared broadcast domain.</p>
        <p><strong>MeshWG (WireGuard) is a Layer 3 IP routing protocol.</strong> It routes IP packets and does not natively pass broadcast traffic. This makes it suited for modern IP workloads such as web applications, SSH, RDP, and standard file sharing.</p>
        
        <h2 id="performance">Performance & Architecture</h2>
        <p>The architectural differences impact how each protocol processes traffic.</p>
        <p>Because WireGuard runs in the Linux kernel on supported platforms, it processes packets natively within the operating system. ZeroTier runs entirely in userspace, which involves additional overhead from userspace processing and Ethernet framing.</p>

        <h2 id="router-support">Router Compatibility</h2>
        <p>Both solutions can be deployed on physical network edge devices, but hardware constraints differ.</p>
        <p>While ZeroTier can run on routers, it often requires specific hardware architectures. For example, on MikroTik routers, ZeroTier is restricted to <a href="https://help.mikrotik.com/docs/display/ROS/ZeroTier" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ARM and ARM64 architectures on RouterOS v7+</a>. Older or different architectures (such as MIPS) may not be natively supported.</p>
        <p>WireGuard is natively integrated into Linux kernel 5.6+ and is supported on OpenWrt and OPNsense, allowing MeshWG to run on those existing hardware platforms.</p>

        <h2 id="financials">Pricing Models</h2>
        <p>ZeroTier's paid plans are billed based on the total device count. As of 2026, ZeroTier's <a href="https://www.zerotier.com/pricing/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Essential plan starts at $18/month</a> (which includes up to 10 devices) and charges $2.00 per month for each additional device.</p>
        <p>MeshWG charges a flat rate per machine (router). Terminating the tunnel at the branch router means that all devices on the local network can access the mesh without requiring individual licenses or endpoint agents, which scales differently for multi-branch physical deployments.</p>

        <h2 id="faq">Frequently asked questions</h2>
        {faqs.map((f) => (<div class="faq-item"><h3>{f.q}</h3><p>{f.a}</p></div>))}

        <div class="next">
          <h2>Next steps</h2>
          <div class="cta-row">
            <a class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" href="https://vpn.meshwg.com/signup">Start free → 2 routers</a>
            <a class="btn btn-line btn-lg" href="/compare/zerotier-vs-wireguard/">ZeroTier vs WireGuard</a>
          </div>
          <p class="related">
            See also:
            <a href="/alternatives/tailscale/">Tailscale Alternative</a> ·
            <a href="/what-is-wireguard/">What is WireGuard?</a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Footer />

  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema)} />
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(breadcrumbSchema)} />
</Base>

<style>
  .guide { padding: 64px 0 128px; }
  .guide .wrap { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 220px 1fr; gap: 56px; align-items: start; }
  .toc { position: sticky; top: 100px; font-size: 13.5px; }
  .toc-h { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.14em; color: var(--text-3); margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .toc ol { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; counter-reset: tocnum; }
  .toc li { counter-increment: tocnum; padding: 8px 0 8px 26px; position: relative; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-faint); line-height: 1.45; }
  .toc li::before { content: counter(tocnum, decimal-leading-zero); position: absolute; left: 0; top: 8px; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px; color: var(--text-4); }
  .toc a { color: var(--text-2); transition: color 0.15s ease; }
  .toc a:hover { color: var(--accent); }
  article { max-width: 820px; }
  .guide h2 { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 28px; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: -0.02em; line-height: 1.15; margin: 56px 0 16px; color: var(--text); text-wrap: balance; scroll-margin-top: 100px; }
  .guide h2:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  .guide h3 { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 18px; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: -0.01em; margin: 24px 0 8px; color: var(--text); }
  .guide p { color: var(--text-2); font-size: 15.5px; line-height: 1.7; margin: 0 0 16px; }
  .guide strong { color: var(--text); font-weight: 600; }
  .guide a { color: var(--accent); }
  .guide a:hover { color: var(--accent-strong); }
  .faq-item { margin: 32px 0; } .faq-item h3 { font-size: 17px; margin-bottom: 10px; }
  .next { margin-top: 64px; padding: 32px 36px; background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius-xl); }
  .next h2 { margin-top: 0; font-size: 24px; }
  .cta-row { display: flex; gap: 12px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin: 18px 0; }
  .related { font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-3); margin-top: 24px; }
  .related a { margin: 0 4px; }
  @media (max-width: 980px) { .guide { padding: 32px 0 64px; } .guide .wrap { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 24px; } .toc { position: static; } .guide h2 { font-size: 24px; margin-top: 40px; } .next { padding: 22px 22px; } }
</style>
